    "http://careers.uah.edu/cw/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "Staff Careers",
      "description": "UAH - Staff Careers Skip to main content I am a... Prospective Student Current Student Parent Research Partner Faculty / Staff Member Visit UAH Apply to UAH Request Info Campus Map × search Visit UAH Apply to UAH Request Info Campus Map Home Admission & Aid Academics Research Life at UAH Athletics News Staff Careers Applicant Login Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Follow Human Resources Applicant Login Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Business Intelligence Analyst Alabama The Business Intelligence (BI) Analyst supports the university’s mission by transforming complex data into actionable insights that drive student success, operational excellence, and informed strategic decisions. This position works collaboratively across campus to translate business needs into technical solutions, enhance enterprise systems such as Ellucian Banner, and promote a culture of data-informed decision-making throughout the institution. Donor Relations Coordinator Alabama 9 Sep 2026 The Donor Relations Coordinator plays a vital role in supporting the Division's initiatives related to donor stewardship and engagement. This position works in collaboration with the Director of Advancement Services and the Advancement Team to optimize the donor experience through engagement initiatives and reporting. The incumbent works closely with leadership and stakeholders to strengthen donor relationships and further the Division's advancement goals. Staff Assistant Alabama The Staff Assistant provides administrative and operational support to the Department Chair, faculty, staff, and students. The incumbent assists with the department's day-to-day operations, including academic scheduling, departmental records, events, faculty and student support, and other university business as assigned. Desktop Engineer I Alabama The Desktop Engineer I is a mid-level technical role responsible for the engineering, implementation, and delivery of advanced, proactive end-user support services across the university. This position requires expertise in desktop operating systems, endpoint hardware, enterprise software, cybersecurity protocols, and emerging support technologies. The Desktop Engineer I delivers exceptional service to faculty, staff, and students while actively contributing to service improvement, security posture, and operational efficiency within a dynamic and high-expectation environment. The incumbent will develop tools that can be used by end-users on a larger scale, designed to meet organization, college, or campus-wide requirements. Senior HRIS & Compliance Analyst Alabama Reporting to the Director for HR Innovation and Technology, with a dotted-line reporting relationship to the Manager for Benefits and Employee Services, this position provides cross-functional HRIS, benefits, and employee services support by assuming recurring operational, data, reporting, system, and vendor-related responsibilities. Upon hire, the incumbent will maintain day-to-day operations while key staff dedicate significant time to the ERP implementation. Research Scientist II, S 1-4 Alabama The Research Scientist II will serve as task lead over various processes and be responsible for data analysis, extracting, validating, and cataloguing vital metadata from complex, large-scale Earth Science NASA scientific data collections.\n\nKey responsibilities include\n\n• Serve as the Task Lead for cloud data ingestion activities by planning, coordinating, and overseeing the integration, validation, optimization, and continuous improvement of data pipelines from multiple sources, ensuring data quality, system performance, and compliance with organizational standards while supporting analytics, reporting, and operational requirements.\n• Serve as team lead and manage data quality control and troubleshooting efforts by overseeing routine quality assurance reviews of metadata records, identifying and resolving data discrepancies, collaborating with data producers to implement corrective actions, and ensuring data integrity, consistency, and adherence to established standards.\n• Manage and oversee the data publication and documentation process by coordinating the ingestion, validation, publication, and maintenance of metadata records, ensuring accurate documentation, data integrity, compliance with organizational standards, and the timely availability of information for stakeholders.\n• Lead and oversee the design, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance of scripts and software solutions that automate business and operational processes, ensuring reliability, scalability, system performance, and adherence to organizational standards Computer Scientist I,S1 Alabama The Computer Scientist will provide data analytics support for DoD-funded research efforts.\n\nKey Responsibilities Include\n\n• Provide data analytics support for DoD-funded research efforts.\n• Research and analyze pricing data for military facilities and components to support cost evaluation and budget planning.\n• Mentor undergraduate students regarding data analytics for military systems. Computer Scientist I, S1 Alabama 8 Sep 2026 The Computer Scientist will perform research and provide engineering expertise in the areas of ephemeral computing environments and API-based data integration.\n\nKey Responsibilities Include\n• Perform research, design, implement, and maintain API codebase with a focus on robust interface architecture and reliable data flow.\n• Analyze source schemas and API documentation to write data maps and convert raw structures into functional metadata models.\n• Define operating models, standard access patterns, and support processes for ephemeral computing environments.\n• Monitor system availability metrics and log operational telemetry across data pipelines.\n• Deploy and manage containerized software components to support scalable, isolated execution within ephemeral environments.\n\nMinimum Requirements Include\n• Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or Information Systems  \n• 0 - 12 months of directly related full-time work experience.  \n• Knowledge of software engineering processes and software development workflows.\n• U.S. Citizenship is required Student Accounts Coordinator Alabama The University of Alabama in Huntsville is seeking a Student Accounts Coordinator within the Office of the Bursar. This role is vital in managing the accounts management and reconciliation and NFLP processes and procedures. Processes will include student accounts and facilitating funding from third-party agencies to support students' educational goals. Responsibilities include overseeing student account sponsorships, billing, collecting, and reconciling funds from external agencies for tuition, fees, and other charges. The Student Accounts Coordinator provides excellent customer service through the call center, email, and in-person service, helping students understand their accounts and sponsor billing procedures. This position requires adherence to policies and regulations, attention to detail, teamwork, and strong organizational skills to manage competing priorities. The Coordinator will also assist in reconciling accounts to the general ledger and perform other duties as assigned to ensure the highest level of service for students, parents, faculty, and staff. Maintenance Technician II Alabama The Maintenance Technician II is responsible for the general operation of HVAC, electrical, plumbing, and maintenance in the residential housing facilities at UAH. The Tech II will also help with the removal and moving of furniture throughout the facilities. Research Associate IV Alabama The Research Associate IV will be responsible for performing comprehensive research, data analysis, and metadata extraction. Research Associate V, Step 1-4 Alabama We are currently seeking a Research Associate to provide support to NASA Earth Action science and application activities related to the development of the NASA Disasters Program Portal. The NASA Disasters Portal is dedicated to advancing the awareness, discoverability/access, understanding, and application of Earth science information for disaster management communities. Experience with developing scientific training, organizing and executing scientific workshops, and interfacing across various federal and state government agencies is strongly desired for this position. The position will be located at the National Space Science & Technology Center in Huntsville, Alabama. After School Care Assistant Alabama The UAH Early Learning Center blends best practices from early childhood education, child development, early childhood special education, and integrated therapy to give all children a firm foundation for their future. The learning environment is designed to promote and allow for multidimensional growth: socially, cognitively, physically, and emotionally. The selected candidate will be working within the RISE School, which strives to provide a curriculum that fosters self-confidence, self-esteem, independence, and curiosity within an inclusive environment that brings together traditional learners and learners with exceptional needs.\n\nThe After School Care Assistant works under the general direction of the Director. The Lead Childcare Assistant oversees scheduling and lesson planning. The After School Care Assistant independently manages the learning environment in their assigned classroom. The Lead Childcare Assistant has the ultimate responsibility for the classroom environment. However, the incumbent works closely with the Lead to maintain an appropriate learning environment. Research Associate IV, Step 1 Alabama The selected Research Associate candidate will support the Office of Data Science and Informatics (ODSI) within the Lab for Applied Science (LAS) under the Earth System Science Center (ESSC) at UAH. This role focuses on advancing data science capabilities to support NASA Earth science data management, access, and dissemination.\n\nODSI evaluates trends across data science and informatics communities to inform strategic direction and develop effective, scalable solutions. The office also provides a user-centered perspective on how Earth science data are represented, communicated, and utilized. The position contributes to cross-disciplinary collaboration aimed at improving all phases of the Earth science data lifecycle, including policy, engineering, workflows, and information delivery. Wraparound Classroom Assistant and Daytime Floater Alabama The Wraparound Classroom Assistant and Daytime Floater will function in two primary roles: 1) as a substitute teacher/caregiver during the UAH Early Learning Center's primary daytime program (8:00 am - 2:30 pm) when full-time teaching staff are absent, or providing extra assistance in classrooms when full-time staff are present, and 2) as the lead caregiver in a wraparound program classroom (7:00 - 8:00 am and/or 2:30 - 5:30 pm).\n\nPosition duties may involve feeding children, diapering, and/or assisting with potty training, administering basic first aid for injuries, and interacting with and ensuring the safety and well-being of all children, including those with special needs. Teacher's Assistant Alabama The UAH Early Learning Center blends best practices from early childhood education, child development, early childhood special education, and integrated therapy to give all children a firm foundation for their future. The learning environment is designed to promote and allow for multidimensional growth: socially, cognitively, physically, and emotionally. The selected candidate will be working within the RISE School, which strives to provide a curriculum that fosters self-confidence, self-esteem, independence, and curiosity within an inclusive environment that brings together traditional learners and learners with exceptional needs.\n\nThe Teacher's Assistant will provide support for the lead teacher in providing intentional and purposeful interactions with all children, implementation of classroom instruction, and introduction of developmentally appropriate activities in a child-centered, inclusive classroom. Research Program Manager I Alabama The EarthRISE Project Office, within the Lab for Applied Science (LAS) under the Earth System Science Center (ESSC), is seeking an experienced solutions manager to support science teams across EarthRISE in the co-development and implementation of Earth observation (EO)- based solutions for state, tribes, territories, local government, and private sector partners and in the coordination of EarthRISE initiatives across the NASA Earth Science Division.\n\nThe position will complement a large and dynamic applied sciences group, and, as a core member of the EarthRISE Project Office, this position will provide activity and solution management expertise. This includes supporting concept design and development, internal NASA collaboration, stakeholder outreach and engagement, project monitoring, and impact reporting. The incumbent will have knowledge of applied Earth Science, strong project management skills, and a desire to provide leadership and strategic planning to achieve NASA and EarthRISE goals. A strong background in applied Earth Science with knowledge of Earth observation technology, as well as practical experience in coordinating or managing diverse teams, is required.\n\nWhile based in Huntsville, Alabama, the Solutions Manager will provide project management support across multiple NASA centers with stakeholders across the United States. This includes coordination with NASA research scientists, partners, and subject matter experts to manage project progression. The incumbent will also work closely with NASA to design, review, and provide feedback on project concepts and work plans. The incumbent must effectively represent the EarthRISE Project Office and NASA MSFC in a variety of venues, including with stakeholders and at professional conferences and meetings. The candidate will be expected to maintain professional development activities relevant to their work, as well as to build or refine other skillsets as necessary and required for the position.\n\nOperating within Earth Action, the EarthRISE project office focuses on developing last-mile solutions, improving coordinated action across NASA Earth Science, and fostering workforce development. EarthRISE is actively involved in developing applications in water resources, agriculture, and their critical intersection to support state, local, tribal, territorial, and private sector stakeholders.\n\nEarthRISE is a project of the National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) that works in collaboration with state, local, tribal, territorial, and private sector partners to use information provided by Earth observing satellites and geospatial technologies for managing environmental challenges EarthRISE’s goal is to empower decision-makers with tools, products, geospatial artificial intelligence, and services to act locally on issues such as disasters, agriculture, water, ecosystems, air quality, and health.\n\nThe EarthRISE Project Office in Huntsville, AL, offers a flexible and dynamic work environment, with an in-house team of over 30 science professionals and numerous opportunities for growth and professional development. With a growing economy, diverse population, low cost of living, and vibrant city life, Huntsville is consistently ranked among the top places to live in the U.S. Principal Research Scientist IV, S2 Alabama The purpose of this position is to provide technical leadership and operational oversight for the research, development, design, testing, and characterization of advanced disruptor technologies and explosive systems. The role is responsible for planning, executing, and managing complex experimental programs involving fluid jets, shock waves, internal and terminal ballistics, and explosive tools. This position ensures the successful design and implementation of test configurations, instrumentation, and data acquisition, and delivers high-quality technical documentation, reports, and presentations to government sponsors and technical stakeholders. As the organizational subject matter expert in disruptor technologies and characterization, the incumbent drives innovation, supports mission-critical research objectives, and ensures technical excellence in experimental testing and analysis. Custodian Alabama The Custodian is a key member of the UAH Facilities & Operations department, which is responsible for the planning, design, construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair of the University. As a Custodian, the employee's primary responsibility is to maintain the cleanliness of the University's buildings. The employee’s duties will be performed full-time within the first shift (5:00 AM - 1:45 PM). Custodian Alabama The Custodian is a key member of the UAH Facilities & Operations department, which is responsible for the planning, design, construction, renovation, maintenance, and repair of the University. As a Custodian, the employee's primary responsibility is to maintain the cleanliness of the University's buildings. The employee’s duties will be performed full-time within the hours 10:00 AM - 6:45 PM. More Jobs 39 Expression of Interest ESSC Researcher Expression of Interest UAH’s Lab for Applied Science (LAS) is dedicated to scientific discovery and societal impact through the application of Earth observations. We provide multi-disciplinary subject matter expertise, technical team management, and logistical coordination services to program offices at NASA’s Marshall Space Flight Center and across the federal, state, and commercial sectors. Our team employs advanced techniques in data science and novel approaches to capacity building to further the state of the art using remote sensing and geospatial technology. Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Business Intelligence Analyst Alabama The Business Intelligence (BI) Analyst supports the university’s mission by transforming complex data into actionable insights that drive student success, operational excellence, and informed strategic decisions. This position works collaboratively across campus to translate business needs into technical solutions, enhance enterprise systems such as Ellucian Banner, and promote a culture of data-informed decision-making throughout the institution. Donor Relations Coordinator Alabama Sep 9 2026 The Donor Relations Coordinator plays a vital role in supporting the Division's initiatives related to donor stewardship and engagement. This position works in collaboration with the Director of Advancement Services and the Advancement Team to optimize the donor experience through engagement initiatives and reporting. The incumbent works closely with leadership and stakeholders to strengthen donor relationships and further the Division's advancement goals. Staff Assistant Alabama The Staff Assistant provides administrative and operational support to the Department Chair, faculty, staff, and students. The incumbent assists with the department's day-to-day operations, including academic scheduling, departmental records, events, faculty and student support, and other university business as assigned. Desktop Engineer I Alabama The Desktop Engineer I is a mid-level technical role responsible for the engineering, implementation, and 